# ── AyShCXR .gitignore ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The working directory is ~45GB. Almost all of that is datasets and model
# weights, which do not belong in git. What IS committed: ~1.5MB of code, the
# small JSON files the app needs at runtime, and the documentation.

# ── Datasets (~44GB) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NIH ChestX-ray14, downloaded separately — see docs/
images_0*/
data/vindr/
data/*.csv
data/*.npy
data/*.txt
*.tar
*.zip

# ── Model weights ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 923MB of checkpoints. Too large for git and not redistributable under the
# CheXpert / NIH data licences. Released separately if at all.
models/
*.pth
*.pt
*.onnx
*.tflite

# ── Environments ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
.venv-app/
venv/
env/
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── Generated outputs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
results/*.npz
results/chexpert_preds.npz
data/test_cases/
*.log
nohup.out
ayshcxr_report_*.txt

# KEEP these — the app reads them at startup and will not work without them:
#   results/calibration.json         per-disease temperature scaling
#   results/disease_thresholds.json  per-finding decision thresholds
#   results/finding_baselines.json   baselines for salience ranking
!results/*.json

# ── Secrets — never commit ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GitHub is scraped for these within minutes of a push.
kaggle.json
.kaggle/
*.pem
*.key
.env
credentials*
secrets*

# ── Editor / OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
_*.txt
_*.png
doc_backups/
readme_upload/
REORG_MANIFEST.csv
.claude/launch.json

# ── Archive — internal history, not for publication ─────────────────────────
# archive/snapshot_2026-08-04/ is a frozen copy of the project as it was on
# 4 Aug. Its app.py still contains claims later found to be false (an
# arithmetically impossible AUC of 1.1257, and a "validated ablation" that was
# label leakage). Those are documented in its DO_NOT_USE_README, but an
# unmarked copy of false claims in a public repository is a liability.
# It also carries ~40MB of duplicated label CSVs.
archive/

# ── Third-party PDFs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Published papers by other authors — not ours to redistribute, and large.
docs/*.pdf
